{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1160645-freehold-campaign-help-austin-tx","id":1160645,"title":"Freehold/Campaign help, Austin TX","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-19T14:06:48-08:00","id":1160645,"title":"Freehold/Campaign help, Austin TX","content":"Hello hivemind, I'm hoping I can draw upon your vast resources to help me develop setting and plot for a PbP C:tL game I'm going to be launching in the near future, set in Austin, Texas. In so many ways it seems to me like an archetypal setting for Changeling. It has:<br /> <br /> A legendary festival/live music culture. <br /> A long-standing reputation for being unique, eclectic, and downright weird, with the attendant x2 multiplier for being in the middle of Texas. Lots of anxiety over the gradual loss of that uniqueness as more and more people seek to consume/cash in on it.<br /> A pretty awesome natural environment, including a <i>ton</i> of natural caves and caverns, and lots and lots of water features and green space.<br /> The world's largest urban bat colony, smack in the middle of downtown.<br /> A history of dramatic violence- home of America's first ever celebrity serial killer, the &quot;Servant Girl Annihilator&quot;, as well as the Charles Whitman sniper attacks, and the 2010 plane-crash attack on the IRS offices.<br /> Iconic purple sunsets, which led author O. Henry to dub it &quot;City of the Violet Crown&quot; (c'mon, how changeling is that?). Local lore claims that the purple clouds are caused by lithium in the atmosphere, which accounts for the general wackiness and good-spiritedness of the city.<br /> A long history of growing pains. Housing and infrastructure is never able to keep pace with growth and commercial development, leading to significant problems with homelessness.<br /> Some important formal institutions- the seat of the state government, and the University of Texas. There is some pretty weird history behind Austin's tenure as state capitol- see the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Texas_Archive_War\" target=\"_blank\">Archives War</a>.<br /> A good selection of hauntings and urban legends.<br /> <br /> So lots of props and scenery to work with. The major themes I want to develop are the problem of being a victim of one's own success, growing pains, change and growth vs. memory and tradition, commodification, stuff like that.<br /> <br /> I've worked out a rough court structure:<br /> Court of the Plow- growth, development, wealth, ambition.<br /> Court of the Tower- prestige, reputation, leadership, pride.<br /> Court of the Clouds- fantasy, visions, strangeness, wonder.<br /> Court of the Streams- play, pleasure, conviviality, joy.<br /> Court of the Caverns- secrets, memory, jealousy, protectiveness.<br /> (Streams and Clouds might need to be consolidated into 1 court- not sure about this).<br /> <br /> I haven't figured out a good Bulwark yet- I don't want something too tacky or obvious, like basing it around SXSW. I'm also still trying to figure out the basic political structure of the Freehold. I'm leaning away from a rotating court leadership like the Seasonal courts- I want to play up the antagonism between the &quot;artificial&quot; courts (Plow and Tower) and &quot;natural&quot; courts (Clouds, Streams, and Caverns).<br /> Also trying to work out what kind of changeling population I want. The metro area has a population of about 2 million, a little less than a million in Austin proper. I'm thinking about 30-40 Lost for the freehold all together?<br /> <br /> Also having a hard time figuring out exactly what I want the major conflict/antagonists to be for the campaign. I'm leaning toward a Loyalist conspiracy of some kind, one that's seductive rather than threatening. Once I have players and character concepts, I'll probably have more to work with, but I'd like to have a default of some kind in place.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts, suggestions, insightful questions would be greatly appreciated- particularly in building the Mantle effects and Contracts for the Courts. Cheers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22980-robothedino","name":"robothedino","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}